WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.182
Future:

2
00:00:01.462 --> 00:00:02.849
Plans and Promises.

3
00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:06.585
Day 8 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

4
00:00:08.335 --> 00:00:09.359
The key idea.

5
00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:15.740
Today's goal: talk about plans, predictions, promises and arrangements, and ask people about theirs.

6
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:17.943
Part 1.

7
00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:20.165
Three ways to talk about the future.

8
00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:22.780
Here is a quick table:

9
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.961
Form, and Use for, and Example. will + verb.

10
00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:29.847
Use for: decisions now, promises, offers, predictions.

11
00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:31.001
Example:

12
00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:32.391
I'll call you back.

13
00:00:32.671 --> 00:00:34.889
It will rain later. going to + verb.

14
00:00:35.169 --> 00:00:38.284
Use for: plans you already decided; clear evidence.

15
00:00:38.564 --> 00:00:39.439
Example:

16
00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:41.660
I'm going to buy a new laptop.

17
00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.289
Look at those clouds, it's going to rain. present continuous.

18
00:00:45.569 --> 00:00:48.833
Use for: fixed arrangements (time or place agreed).

19
00:00:49.113 --> 00:00:49.988
Example:

20
00:00:50.268 --> 00:00:52.380
I'm meeting the client at 3 tomorrow.

21
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.516
We're flying to Delhi on Friday.

22
00:00:55.866 --> 00:00:57.231
Part 2. will.

23
00:00:58.481 --> 00:00:59.847
Here is a quick table:

24
00:01:00.127 --> 00:01:02.345
Positive, and Negative, and Question.

25
00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:03.863
I'll send it today.

26
00:01:04.143 --> 00:01:05.039
Negative:

27
00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:06.812
I won't (will not) be late.

28
00:01:07.092 --> 00:01:07.967
Question:

29
00:01:08.247 --> 00:01:09.228
Will you be there?

30
00:01:09.508 --> 00:01:10.852
It'll be ready by 5.

31
00:01:11.132 --> 00:01:12.028
Negative:

32
00:01:12.308 --> 00:01:13.503
It won't take long.

33
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:14.657
Question:

34
00:01:14.937 --> 00:01:16.153
When will it be ready?

35
00:01:17.503 --> 00:01:18.869
Promises and offers:

36
00:01:19.149 --> 00:01:20.386
I'll fix it tonight.

37
00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:21.903
I'll help you with that.

38
00:01:22.183 --> 00:01:23.314
Shall I book a cab?

39
00:01:23.594 --> 00:01:26.218
(Shall I or we = offer or suggestion.).

40
00:01:27.568 --> 00:01:29.125
Part 3. going to.

41
00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:31.741
Here is a quick table:

42
00:01:32.021 --> 00:01:34.239
Positive, and Negative, and Question.

43
00:01:34.519 --> 00:01:36.055
We're going to move to Pune.

44
00:01:36.335 --> 00:01:37.231
Negative:

45
00:01:37.511 --> 00:01:39.261
I'm not going to take the job.

46
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:40.415
Question:

47
00:01:40.695 --> 00:01:42.039
Are you going to apply?

48
00:01:43.389 --> 00:01:44.307
Part 4.

49
00:01:44.587 --> 00:01:46.208
Talking about plans and time.

50
00:01:47.458 --> 00:02:02.071
this evening or weekend, next week or month or year, in two days or an hour. tomorrow morning, the day after tomorrow, by Friday (= not later than Friday). until 6 (= continuing up to 6), soon, later today.

51
00:02:03.421 --> 00:02:04.381
Part 5.

52
00:02:04.661 --> 00:02:06.027
Questions about plans.

53
00:02:07.277 --> 00:02:08.791
What are you doing this weekend?

54
00:02:09.071 --> 00:02:10.949
Are you going to take any leave this year?

55
00:02:11.229 --> 00:02:12.701
When will you know the result?

56
00:02:12.981 --> 00:02:14.538
Will you be free after lunch?

57
00:02:14.818 --> 00:02:16.503
What time are you leaving tomorrow?

58
00:02:17.853 --> 00:02:18.792
Part 6.

59
00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.312
Conversation: planning a weekend trip.

60
00:02:22.562 --> 00:02:24.589
Here is how the conversation goes.

61
00:02:24.869 --> 00:02:26.874
Are you doing anything this weekend?

62
00:02:27.154 --> 00:02:27.879
Yes!

63
00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:30.591
We're going to Coorg on Saturday morning.

64
00:02:30.871 --> 00:02:31.917
Nice!

65
00:02:32.197 --> 00:02:33.626
How are you getting there?

66
00:02:33.906 --> 00:02:35.079
We're driving.

67
00:02:35.359 --> 00:02:37.941
We're going to leave at six to avoid traffic.

68
00:02:38.221 --> 00:02:39.458
Where are you staying?

69
00:02:40.808 --> 00:02:42.408
The conversation continues.

70
00:02:42.688 --> 00:02:44.693
We've booked a homestay near Madikeri.

71
00:02:44.973 --> 00:02:47.235
We're coming back on Sunday evening.

72
00:02:47.515 --> 00:02:48.645
Sounds lovely.

73
00:02:48.925 --> 00:02:50.163
Will it be cold?

74
00:02:50.443 --> 00:02:51.424
Probably.

75
00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.389
I'll pack some jackets.

76
00:02:53.669 --> 00:02:54.928
Send me photos!

77
00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.168
I will.

78
00:02:56.448 --> 00:02:58.432
I'll message you when we get there.

79
00:02:59.782 --> 00:03:00.721
Part 7.

80
00:03:01.001 --> 00:03:01.918
Practice.

81
00:03:03.168 --> 00:03:05.920
1. will, going to, or present continuous?

82
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:06.819
A:

83
00:03:07.099 --> 00:03:08.251
The phone is ringing.

84
00:03:08.531 --> 00:03:09.213
B:

85
00:03:09.493 --> 00:03:10.603
I (answer) it.

86
00:03:10.883 --> 00:03:12.845
We (visit) my parents next Sunday.

87
00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.149
It's all planned.

88
00:03:14.429 --> 00:03:16.157
I promise I (not tell) anyone.

89
00:03:16.437 --> 00:03:17.483
I've decided:

90
00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.661
I (learn) Kubernetes this year.

91
00:03:21.011 --> 00:03:21.929
Success:

92
00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:23.062
Answers.

93
00:03:23.342 --> 00:03:27.715
'll answer 2. are visiting (or are going to visit) 3. won't tell 4.

94
00:03:27.995 --> 00:03:29.190
'm going to learn.

95
00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.244
2.

96
00:03:31.524 --> 00:03:32.612
Make questions.

97
00:03:32.892 --> 00:03:39.335
(you or do or tonight or what), (the results or be or ready or when), (you or apply or for the job).

98
00:03:40.685 --> 00:03:41.602
Success:

99
00:03:41.882 --> 00:03:42.735
Answers.

100
00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:44.317
What are you doing tonight?

101
00:03:44.597 --> 00:03:46.218
When will the results be ready?

102
00:03:46.498 --> 00:03:48.247
Are you going to apply for the job?

103
00:03:49.597 --> 00:03:50.344
3.

104
00:03:50.624 --> 00:03:56.640
Write 3 plans for next week: one with going to, one arrangement with time, one promise with will.

105
00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:58.865
Part 8.

106
00:03:59.145 --> 00:04:00.190
Speak today.

107
00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.467
Tell someone your plans for this weekend.

108
00:04:03.747 --> 00:04:05.731
Make one promise at work with a time:

109
00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:07.653
I'll send it by 4 pm.

110
00:04:07.933 --> 00:04:09.427
Offer help with Shall I...?

111
00:04:10.777 --> 00:04:12.313
That's the end of this lesson.

112
00:04:12.593 --> 00:04:17.265
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

113
00:04:17.545 --> 00:04:23.646
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

